#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
shtop - Shell Top: zero-root system & GPU monitor for Linux.

The Linux twin of ptop (PowerShell Top): same layout, themes and controls.
A single file, Python 3 standard library only, no root required. Reads /proc
and /sys directly; NVIDIA telemetry comes from nvidia-smi when present, AMD
from amdgpu sysfs, and per-process GPU activity for AMD/Intel from DRM fdinfo.

Controls:
  [Q] / [Esc] : Quit (Esc clears an active filter first; Ctrl+C also quits)
  [/]         : Filter processes by name or PID (Enter keeps, Esc clears)
  [Up]/[Down] : Select process in table
  [K] / [Del] : Send SIGTERM to selected process (press again within 3s: SIGKILL)
  [P]         : Toggle Per-Core CPU bars view
  [T]         : Cycle color themes (Midnight, Cyberpunk, Matrix, Gruvbox, Nord)
  [C]         : Sort processes by CPU%
  [M]         : Sort processes by Memory
  [G]         : Prioritize GPU processes
  [+] / [-]   : Increase / Decrease refresh speed
"""

